Check that the list covers the regulations in the compliance register, that the contact details are up to date, and that the people who contact authorities know where the list is.

{{#if this.craGuidance}}
== EU Cyber Resilience Act

Under the CRA (Regulation (EU) 2024/2847), the manufacturer of a product with digital elements sends its notifications through the single reporting platform to ENISA and to the CSIRT designated as coordinator in the Member State where it has its main establishment in the EU (Articles 14 and 16). Add the single reporting platform and this CSIRT to the list.

Also add the market surveillance authorities of the Member States where the products are placed on the market. On a reasoned request, the manufacturer must give them the information and the documentation that show the conformity of the product (Article 13).
